# Conformance run output. Generated, not authored.
#
# A run is a measurement of the ADR set at one substrate SHA, with one model, on
# one date. It is reproducible from the cases plus that SHA, so committing it
# would version an artefact that can be regenerated, and would bury the cases
# under churn every time the suite runs.
#
# What survives a run is the finding, not the transcript: a gap, a conflict, or
# an agreement rate that moved. Those are written into the case file or into a
# record, both of which are tracked.
# Ignore the contents, not the directory. Excluding `runs/` itself would stop git
# descending into it, and a negation cannot re-include a file whose parent is excluded.
runs/*
!runs/.gitkeep
